(A RECONSTRUCTION OF PROTO-TANGKHULIC RHYMES) Tj
0 -19 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Authors: David R. Mortensen, James A. Miller) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Journal/Venue: Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area \(LTBA\) | Year: 2013) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Subject: Historical Phonology & Sino-Tibetan Rhymes | Language: English & Tangkhul) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 11 Tf
(ABSTRACT:) Tj
0 -15 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(We reconstruct the rhyme system of Proto-Tangkhulic \(PTk\) based on a) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(comparative corpus of over 800 cognate sets spanning Standard Tangkhul) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(\(Ukhrul\), Huishu, Kachai, Champhung, and Tusom. We demonstrate that) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Proto-Tangkhulic distinguished phonemic vowel length before dental and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(velar codas \(*-a:t vs *-at; *-a:k vs *-ak\), and retained the Proto-) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tibeto-Burman lateral coda *-l, which merged into front glides or open) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(vowels in Standard Tangkhul. This reconstruction resolves longstanding) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(anomalies in the external comparison of Tangkhul with Jingpho and Lolo-) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Burmese.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Keywords: Rhymes, Proto-Tangkhulic, Tibeto-Burman, Vowel Length, Liquid Codas, LTBA) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
endstream
