(1. THE PTK RHYME INVENTORY) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(The reconstructed rhyme inventory of Proto-Tangkhulic includes 24) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(distinct rhymes with stop and nasal codas: *-am, *-an, *-ang, *-ap, *-at,) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(*-ak, *-a:t, *-a:k, *-im, *-in, *-ing, *-ip, *-it, *-ik, *-um, *-un,) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(*-ung, *-up, *-ut, *-uk, and lateral rhymes *-al, *-il, *-ul. While) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Standard Tangkhul regularly neutralizes vowel length before codas, the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(conservative Huishu dialect preserves qualitative differences that) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(verify the length distinction.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * kapik \(Ukhrul\) / pi:k \(Huishu\) : to sleep) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Reflects PTk *Ce-pi:k \(long vowel before velar stop\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * kashak \(Ukhrul\) / sa' \(Kachai\) : to eat) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: PTk *Ce-syak \(short rhyme with glottal realization\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * tui \(Ukhrul\) / tul \(Huishu\) : speech, language) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: PTk *to:l \(preservation of final lateral in Huishu\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
ET
endstream
