(2. EVOLUTION OF LATERAL CODAS \(*-L\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(One of the major breakthroughs of Proto-Tangkhulic historical phonology) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(is recognizing the regular fate of PTB *-l. In Standard Ukhrul, PTB *-l) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(vocalized to a high front offglide [-i] after back vowels \(e.g. *tul >) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(tui 'speech'; *ngul > ngui 'silver/money'\). In Huishu, *-l is preserved) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(intact as an alveolar lateral continuant [-l], proving that lateral loss) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(in Ukhrul was a secondary innovation of the central dialect group.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * ngui \(Ukhrul\) / ngul \(Huishu\) : silver, coin, money) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Direct cognate with Written Tibetan dngul.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * kahui \(Ukhrul\) / hul \(Huishu\) : to bark \(of dog\)) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Reflects PTB *hwel.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * malui \(Ukhrul\) / melol \(Huishu\) : to forget) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Preservation of liquid coda in archaic peripheral varieties.) Tj
0 -12 Td
ET
