(3. IMPLICATIONS FOR SINO-TIBETAN SUBGROUPING) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Recognizing the conservative nature of Proto-Tangkhulic rhymes provides) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(a crucial benchmark for the genetic classification of the Indo-Burma) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(borderlands. Tangkhulic shares specific rhyme mergers with Maring and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Kuki-Chin, yet preserves distinct prefixal morphology that establishes) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(it as a primary coordinate branch of Tibeto-Burman.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
